Iran's military said overnight it has  not lost any drones after President  Trump said a u.s. warship destroyed his  word an Iranian drone in a defensive  action this comes as the top US military  commander for the Middle East general  Frank Mackenzie is traveling in the  region and our David Martin is the only  TV correspondent with him Mackenzie was  in Saudi Arabia to build support for a  force to protect vital oil shipments  David Martin reports from Jeddah  Pentagon says the USS boxer took  defensive action when an Iranian drone  came within 1,000 yards the boxer is an  amphibious assault ship part of a fleet  deployed to the Persian Gulf to patrol  shipping orders the u.s. accuses Iran of  interfering with an accusation president  Trump repeated when he announced the  drone had been brought down this is the  latest of many provocative and hostile  actions by Iran against vessels  operating in international waters the  downing came less than a month after  Iran shot down an American drones  prompting the u.s. to prepare a  retaliatory strike which President Trump  called off at the 11th hour u.s. says it  has compelling evidence Iran is behind  the sabotage and harassment of tankers  passing in and out of the Strait of  Hormuz and most recently Iran allegedly  hijacked a small coastal banker claiming  it was smuggling oil illegally on  Thursday we flew with general Frank  McKenzie the top US commander for the  Middle East into Saudi Arabia McKenzie  is in the region working to organize a  flotilla of warships to escort tankers  in and out of the Gulf but not unless  other countries participate that is an  international responsibility not a  United States responsibility but the  United States is very happy to be part  of the solution but only the US can  provide the airpower to defend against  the  attack the Pentagon is reportedly  sending 500 troops to an airbase in  Saudi Arabia last use during the first  Gulf War now nearly 30 years later there  is the possibility of another war this  time against Iran for CBS this morning  David Martin in Jeddah Saudi Arabia
 

